---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Cordelia ARC – Gabriel Alisasis" description="A California supportive-living agency's marketing site rebuilt into the software the agency runs on: referrals, hiring, compliance, and billing, in React, TypeScript, and Supabase.">
  <div class="page-top-spacer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <section id="case">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="breadcrumb-head">
        <a href="/work">← All work</a>
      </div>
      <div class="case-list">
        <article class="case reveal">
          <div class="case-top">
            <div class="case-shot">
              <div class="chrome">
                <span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span><span class="dot"></span>
                <span class="urlbar">cordeliaarc.com</span>
              </div>
              <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                   alt="Cordelia ARC homepage showing the headline Compassionate Care for Brighter Futures over a photo of a caregiver with a client">
            </div>
            <div class="case-info">
              <div class="case-idx">Case 01 / 04</div>
              <h3>Cordelia ARC – supportive-living platform, public site to admin back office</h3>
              <p>A California supportive-living agency serving adults with intellectual disabilities across Alameda and Contra Costa counties. What began as a marketing site became the software the agency runs on – referrals, hiring, compliance, and billing.</p>
              <blockquote class="pullquote">The same referral and intake operations I usually automate inside a CRM – this time built as an actual application.</blockquote>
              <dl class="spec">
                <div><dt>Sector</dt><dd>Healthcare · HIPAA-regulated</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Stack</dt><dd>React · TypeScript · Supabase</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Scale</dt><dd>91 migrations · ~50 edge functions</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Surface</dt><dd>40+ routed pages</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="case-actions">
                <a class="visit-btn" href="https://cordeliaarc.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit site ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

            <div class="case-body">
              <div class="pao">
                <div class="pao-col pao-problem">
                  <h4>Problem</h4>
                  <p>The agency ran on disconnected parts: a brochure website, paper onboarding packets, referrals tracked by hand, and compliance documents that had to be printed, signed, and scanned back. Nothing talked to anything else, and every new hire meant re-keying the same details into a dozen forms.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pao-col pao-approach">
                  <h4>Approach</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Built the public site and the internal platform as <strong>one React + TypeScript application</strong>, so marketing, referrals, and operations share a data layer.</li>
                    <li>Put every privileged action behind <strong>role-based access enforced in Postgres</strong>, not merely hidden in the UI.</li>
                    <li>Moved the paper packet into a browser flow – <strong>PDF form-filling and e-signature</strong>, with phone OTP verification.</li>
                    <li>Pushed integration work into <strong>Supabase edge functions</strong> so the front-end never holds a third-party secret.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="pao-col pao-outcome">
                  <h4>Outcome</h4>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>91 database migrations</strong> and <strong>~50 edge functions</strong> in production.</li>
                    <li><strong>40+ routed pages</strong> spanning the public site, a compliance portal, and the admin back office.</li>
                    <li>Referrals, HR, compliance, and billing run in one system instead of four.</li>
                    <li>Onboarding is a link, not a packet.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="diagram-wrap">
                <div class="cap">Fig. 02 – architecture, request path</div>
                <svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 900 250" role="img"
                     aria-label="Architecture diagram: a React single-page app calls Supabase Auth with role-based access, which reaches about fifty edge functions, which reach Postgres with ninety-one migrations and row-level security. Below, five modules branch off: referrals pipeline, compliance portal, HR and applications, billing, and outbound integrations.">
                  <text class="dg-head" x="8" y="16">CLIENT</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="26" width="200" height="62"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="22" y="50">React SPA</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="22" y="66">Vite · TypeScript · Tailwind</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="22" y="79">shadcn/ui · TanStack Query</text>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="232" y="16">GATEWAY</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-accent" x="232" y="26" width="200" height="62"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="246" y="50">Supabase Auth</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="246" y="66">role-based access</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="246" y="79">admin · staff · applicant</text>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="456" y="16">LOGIC</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box" x="456" y="26" width="200" height="62"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="470" y="50">Edge Functions</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="470" y="66">~50 deployed</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="470" y="79">Deno · server-side keys</text>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="680" y="16">DATA</text>
                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-accent" x="680" y="26" width="200" height="62"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="694" y="50">Postgres</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="694" y="66">91 migrations</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="694" y="79">row-level security</text>

                  <path class="dg-flow" style="--len:24" d="M208 57 L232 57"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow" style="--len:24" d="M432 57 L456 57"/>
                  <path class="dg-flow" style="--len:24" d="M656 57 L680 57"/>

                  <text class="dg-head" x="8" y="120">MODULES</text>
                  <path class="dg-line" d="M556 88 L556 116 M90 116 L810 116 M90 116 L90 142 M270 116 L270 142 M450 116 L450 142 M630 116 L630 142 M810 116 L810 142"/>

                  <rect class="dg-box" x="8" y="142" width="164" height="44"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="22" y="163">Referrals pipeline</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="22" y="177">stage-change automation</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box" x="188" y="142" width="164" height="44"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="202" y="163">Compliance portal</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="202" y="177">PDF fill · e-signature</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box" x="368" y="142" width="164" height="44"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="382" y="163">HR &amp; applications</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="382" y="177">offers · background checks</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box" x="548" y="142" width="164" height="44"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="562" y="163">Billing</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="562" y="177">cases · automations</text>

                  <rect class="dg-box dg-box-accent" x="728" y="142" width="164" height="44"/>
                  <text class="dg-label" x="742" y="163">Integrations</text>
                  <text class="dg-sub" x="742" y="177">Google · GHL · Metricool</text>
                </svg>
              </div>

              <div class="stack-row">
                <span class="pill">React</span><span class="pill">TypeScript</span><span class="pill">Vite</span>
                <span class="pill">Tailwind</span><span class="pill">shadcn/ui</span><span class="pill">Supabase</span>
                <span class="pill">Postgres</span><span class="pill">Deno</span><span class="pill">TanStack Query</span>
                <span class="pill">React Hook Form</span><span class="pill">Zod</span><span class="pill">Recharts</span>
              </div>

              <figure class="case-gallery">
                <img class="zoomable" src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     alt="Cordelia ARC services page listing Supportive Living Services, Individual Living Services and Coordinated Family Support as photo cards">
                <figcaption>The public services pages sit on the same codebase as the admin platform – a referral submitted here lands directly in the pipeline board, no re-keying.</figcaption>
              </figure>
            </div>
          
        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
